            "text": "{\n  \"relation\": \"DIVERGENT\",\n  \"consensus_summary\": \"Sapphire symbolizes heavenly glory, the firmament/sky, and the manifest presence or throne of God, derived from its blue color resembling the heavens.\",\n  \"book_summary\": \"Sapphire symbolizes the full moon in its enthroned and bridal form, representing a reflected glory ('a brightness worn, not owned'), and is identified with the tribe of Issachar.\",\n  \"consensus_core_identification\": \"The sky, heaven, and direct divine glory/throne.\",\n  \"book_core_identification\": \"The full moon and its borrowed brightness.\",\n  \"core_relation\": \"CONTRADICTS\",\n  \"extension_relation\": \"DIFFERENT_REFERENT\",\n  \"boundary_disagreement\": \"The consensus applies sapphire broadly to the heavens and direct divine majesty; the book restricts its symbolism specifically to the moon as a celestial body and the tribe of Issachar.\",\n  \"material_contradiction\": \"The consensus links sapphire's 'clearness' to the blue sky and God's inherent glory; the book explicitly denies the sky/heaven identification, linking the 'clearness' to the full moon's reflected glory that can be made to cease.\",\n  \"rationale\": \"The book explicitly rejects the consensus view of sapphire as the 'blue of heaven itself' or direct divine glory, replacing it with a lunar identification based on the concept of 'clearness' as a temporary or borrowed brightness.\",\n  \"citation_support\": \"PARTIAL\",\n  \"strongest_objection\": \"Exodus 24:10 explicitly compares the sapphire pavement to 'the body of heaven in his clearness' (the sky itself). The moon is not inherently blue like a sapphire, and linking the stone to the moon relies on synthesizing distant texts (such as Psalm 89) rather than the immediate visual description of the gem.\",\n  \"confidence\": \"high\"\n}",
